※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4431

※ One element says what an array holds and no other may disagree with it.  That
※ is the other half of the rule: the type is settled by whichever element says
※ it, and an element saying something else is not a value to be widened but a
※ disagreement about what the array is.
※
※ The complaint is about the array and not about one element, which is why it
※ says what the ones before it were: an element is only wrong here relative to
※ the others.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let a := ⟦1u8, 2u16⟧
    0u6
